% For the articles that should appear in the "References I Contributed To" category:
% In addition to usual fields, there are some fields that need to be defined for proper display:
% * "usera"    (compulsory)     -> Category for grouping in the bibliography (set to custom value and declare it in the main document)
% * "addendum" (compulsory)     -> To manually add a number to the ref (forces order instead of sorting by date)
% * "note"     (optional)       -> To add (a), (b), etc. to the reference and manually disambiguate entries
% * "url"      (optional, list) -> Link to the article      -- icon: newspaper
% * "userb"    (optional, list) -> Poster url               -- icon: picture
% * "userc"    (optional, list) -> Video url                -- icon: YouTube
% * "userd"    (optional, list) -> GitHub url               -- icon: GitHub
% * "usere"    (optional, list) -> Prize url                -- icon: trophy
% * "userf"    (optional, list) -> Slides url               -- icon: pictures

% Every one of these fields holds URL(s): each value becomes a clickable icon under the entry
% In particular, "usere" is the *page announcing the prize*, not the name of the prize -- putting
% plain text there would produce a trophy icon pointing nowhere
% They are lists: separate several URLs with commas to get several icons of the same kind,
% e.g. userd = {https://github.com/a/one, https://github.com/a/two}
% Beware of one asymmetry: "url" is a verbatim field for biblatex, so the space after a comma
% is kept and ends up as a "%20" at the start of the next link -- in "url", and only there,
% write the commas without any space: url = {https://a.org/one,https://a.org/two}
% See "lastname2022conference" below for an entry using all of them at once

% Warning: any entry with usera fields that is not declared in the main document will not appear
% You can ommit "addendum", but entries will still be sorted according to it
% To declare a category, use e.g., \addBiblioCategory{book}{B}{Book Chapters}
% If you only declare one category, the letter/addendum will not be used

% You can also choose not to use categories at all
% In that case, just format all entries as indicated below (i.e., remove "usera" and "addendum")
% If no category is declared, all entries will appear in a single list

% For the articles that should appear in the "Other References Cited in this Document" category:
% In addition to usual fields, there are some fields that need to be defined for proper display:
% * "url"   (compulsory) -> Link to the article
% * "note"  (optional)   -> To add (a), (b), etc. to the reference and manually disambiguate entries

% Links are used with the \urlext command
% For those, just set the following fields:
% * "howpublished" (compulsory) -> The website name, to appear in the brackets
% * "title"        (compulsory) -> Showed when hovered
% * "url"          (compulsory) -> The URL of the resource
% * "author"       (optional)   -> To add extra info on author
% * "year"         (optional)   -> To add extra info on publication year
% * "note"         (optional)   -> To add (a), (b), etc. to the reference and manually disambiguate entries

% All entries below are placeholders, kept minimal on purpose
% Replace them with your own, and delete the ones you do not need

